Root cause found and fixed in the polling USART example source.

### What was broken
`usart/usart.c` was missing the USART driver header include, so all USART symbols were undeclared at compile time:
- `usart_set_baudrate`
- `usart_set_databits`
- `USART2`
- `USART_STOPBITS_1`, etc.

This is why the polling example failed while `usart_irq` built: `usart_irq.c` already included the correct header.

### Fix applied
File updated:
- `firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/usart/usart.c`

Change:
```c
#include <libopencm3/stm32/usart.h>
```
added alongside existing RCC/GPIO includes.

### Verification
Rebuilt the polling example with explicit libopencm3 path:
- `make OPENCM3_DIR=/Users/gowthamreddys/Desktop/hydron-evaluation/stm32-pilot/firmware/libopencm3`
- Build now succeeds (no undeclared USART symbol errors).

Also checked `usart_irq` target remains unaffected.
